                <pb facs="0119" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg99"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Benavides, minister of foreign affairs, to Mr.
                        Perry, United States chargé d’affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Madrid,
                                Palace</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22,
                        1865</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><seg type="margin">[473]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to reply to your note of
                    yesterday relative to the enlistment of seamen, which, it is said, the
                    confederate steamer Stonewall has effected at the Ferrol; that the same day I
                    transferred it to the minister of marine for him to *adopt the proper measures
                    to procure that the commander of said vessel should set on shore the men which
                    it seems he has fraudulently embarked.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of the occasion, &amp;c., &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. BENAVIDES.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
